      "title": "Swift 6.4 Released",
      "type": "story",
      "url": "https://www.swift.org/blog/swift-6.4-released/",
      "og_image": "https://swift.org/apple-touch-icon-180x180.png",
      "groq_label": "Swift 6.4 advances WebAssembly compilation and fixes debugger variable visibility issues without focusing on AI features.",
      "groq_discussion": "This product addresses modern programming language tooling and cross-platform software development. Hacker News commenters generally appreciated the progress made in WebAssembly support and believed the project could provide an easier alternative to Rust for web targets. However, they also expressed concerns about historical debugging flaws and questioned whether variable inspection issues had been fully resolved. Overall, the discussion was cautiously optimistic, with commenters recognizing both the project's potential and its limitations.",
      "groq_explain": null
    },
