      "groq_label": "A twenty-dollar 4G mobile hotspot can be converted into a standalone texting device by pairing it with an external physical keyboard.",
      "groq_discussion": "Discussion type: – Short:\n\nThis project addresses the inconvenience of viewing texts and OTPs on standalone 4G wireless hotspots without built-in screens. Hacker News commenters generally appreciated the creative hardware repurposing and integration of the Clicks keyboard and believed the project could serve as a practical standalone dumbphone or mini cyberdeck. However, they also expressed concerns about stock battery life limitations and questioned whether additional battery modifications are needed for long-term everyday use. Overall, the discussion was overwhelmingly positive, with commenters recognizing both the project's potential and its limitations.",
      "groq_explain": null
    },
